  "id": "Compound::DB00975 - Gene::5141",
  "verbalization": "Dipyridamole is implicated in the regulation of 3',5'-cyclic-AMP phosphodiesterase activity through its interaction with Pde7a, Pde7b, and Pde8a, all of which are known to participate in this enzymatic process. The evidence suggests that Dipyridamole binds to these Pde isoforms, thereby modulating their activity. This mechanism implies that Dipyridamole may influence Pde4a through a shared pathway involving the regulation of cyclic AMP hydrolysis. The consistent involvement of Pde4a in the enzymatic activity of these phosphodiesterases, as indicated by the cross-references, suggests a potential functional link between Dipyridamole and Pde4a. The integrated evidence highlights a possible role for Dipyridamole in modulating Pde4a activity through the regulation of cyclic AMP phosphodiesterase activity, although the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
